# MasterPHP

Follow root `AGENTS.md` and the EMW core policies. At session start, inspect the baseline status, roadmap, current PHP skill ledger, and relevant project context.

The developer reports some PHP basics; exact proficiency is unassessed until evidence is reviewed. Do not assume beginner or expert level.

For learning tasks, use `learning/prompts/` and `.opencode/skills/php-mastery/SKILL.md` as the teaching guide. For project tasks, use EMW: retrieve relevant knowledge, assess learning value/risk/proficiency/novelty/complexity, select a collaboration mode, plan, implement incrementally, verify, and separately record delivery and mastery.

Prefer modern typed PHP and explicit reasoning. Use prepared database statements and secure web practices. Never claim tests passed if they were not run. A project completion does not automatically establish PHP mastery.
